        "original_id": "4eb8dde9-9606-5694-8acd-c601158642e3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Cardiospermum, Chestnut, Castanea\n- Plant families: Sapindaceae, Fagaceae\n- Places: American tropics, Indian tropics, African tropics, Northern Hemisphere\n- Concepts: genera, species, native ranges\n\nFacts:\n- Cardiospermum is a genus of about 14 species in the soapberry family Sapindaceae.\n- Cardiospermum is native to the American, Indian, and African tropics.\n- Chestnut is the common name for the genus Castanea.\n- Castanea is a genus of eight or nine species of deciduous trees and shrubs in the beech family Fagaceae.\n- Castanea is native to temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere.",
